{%- comment -%}
  PG Gift Fix: the free R36S case, and nothing else.

  ------------------------------------------------------- THE DEAD GIFT VARIANT

  pg-drawer auto-adds a free case whenever the cart holds a console:

      var GIFT_ID = 49623692247268, GIFT_HANDLE = 'r36s-protective-case-free-gift';

  That variant no longer exists — pg-case-add documented why: the case product's
  "Default Title" variant was replaced by two named ones, and a variant id
  cannot be reassigned. So the free case never lands, and giftSync() re-fires a
  422ing /cart/add.js on every cart mutation.

  The live variants are 49640846426340 ($0.00, "Free with console") and
  49640879063268 ($13.99, "Spare case"). Only the $0 one is ever added here, and
  only as the gift, carrying the `_free_gift: yes` property pg-drawer looks for
  so its own giftSync() finds a gift line and stops retrying.

  ------------------------------------------------------------- EVERY CASE, ONCE

  The pass reads /cart.js and settles the cart into exactly one of these:

    consoles = 0, no gift line          -> nothing
    consoles = 0, gift line present     -> remove it
    consoles >= 1, no gift line         -> add ONE, quantity 1
    consoles >= 1, gift line quantity 1 -> nothing
    consoles >= 1, gift line quantity>1 -> set it back to 1

  One free case per cart, never per console: two consoles still get one. A case
  the shopper adds themselves is the $13.99 variant with no _free_gift property
  and is never touched, counted or removed — someone can buy spare cases with or
  without a console. Nothing else is ever added: the paid variant is not
  referenced anywhere in this file.

  ------------------------------------------------- WHAT THIS FILE NO LONGER DOES

  A previous version wrapped window.fetch to notice cart writes. That broke the
  cart: the theme's own code calls fetch unbound in places, and a native fetch
  invoked with the wrong `this` throws Illegal invocation, so cart requests
  failed and the drawer rendered half empty. It is gone — nothing native is
  patched here. The pass is triggered by the drawer's own DOM changing and by
  add-to-cart clicks, and is rate limited so it cannot hammer /cart.js.

  The FREE GIFT pill's inline text-indent/width (written by pg-drawer's ftFix
  from a pre-webfont measurement, which is what made the purple band overhang)
  are still cleared, since that is DOM-local and cannot affect anything else.

  The drawer refresh IS coalesced, which the fetch wrapper's removal does not
  affect: window.pgDrawerRefresh is pg-drawer's own plain function, not a native
  bound method, so wrapping it cannot throw the way patching fetch did. Several
  files call it on one cart change and the whole-page fetch + innerHTML swaps
  stacked, each discarding the paint before it. Overlapping calls now collapse
  into one, with a single trailing refresh if anyone asked while one was in
  flight.

  THIS FILE'S OWN WRITES ARE BOUNDED. With the drawer still reported as
  flickering, everything here that can cause a repaint is capped rather than
  left to a guard that is only as good as the state it reads:

    - at most ONE gift add per page load. If the add lands and something else
      removes the line again, this does not re-add it and re-refresh in a loop —
      it stops, and the next page view starts fresh;
    - the drawer is refreshed only after that FIRST add, never after the
      quantity or removal corrections, which the drawer repaints itself;
    - the whole pass is skipped once the cart is in the shape it should be in,
      so an idle drawer sees no /cart.js traffic beyond the rate-limited checks.

  ------------------------------------------------------- THE GIFT LINE'S PRICE

  The gift now reads like every other discounted line: $13.99 struck through,
  $0.00 beside it, and the SAVED 100% chip. Two parts to that:

    - the $0 variant carries a compare-at price of $13.99 (set on the product,
      not here), so Shopify itself reports the line as fully discounted and the
      theme's own save maths lands on 100%;
    - pg-drawer hides the chip on the gift line on purpose ("FREE GIFT already
      says it"). Per the owner it comes back, so that rule is overridden.

  The FREE GIFT pill is also pulled to the left edge of the line, under the
  product title, rather than sitting wherever the grid cell placed it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* once the inline overrides are cleared, this is the pill's box, pulled to
     the left edge of the line so it sits under the product title */
  #cart .pg-free-tag,
  body.template-cart .pg-free-tag{
    width:max-content !important;
    text-indent:0 !important;
    padding:6px 12px !important;
    text-align:left !important;
    justify-self:start !important;
    align-self:start !important;
    margin-left:0 !important;
    margin-right:auto !important;
  }
  /* the gift line prices like the others: struck full price, $0.00, SAVED 100% */
  #cart .l4ca > li:has(.pg-free-tag) .pg-save-chip,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li:has(.pg-free-tag) .pg-save-chip{display:inline-block !important}
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgGiftFix) return; window.pgGiftFix = 1;

  var GIFT_VARIANT = 49640846426340;                    /* $0.00 "Free with console" */
  var CASE_HANDLE  = 'r36s-protective-case-free-gift';
  var CONSOLE      = 'handheld-game-console';

  var busy = false, lastRun = 0;

  function post(url, body){
    return fetch(url, {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
      body: JSON.stringify(body)
    });
  }

  var added = false;          /* one gift add per page load, no matter what */

  function refresh(){
    if (window.pgDrawerRefresh){ try { window.pgDrawerRefresh(); } catch (e){} }
  }

  /* one drawer refresh at a time. pg-drawer's refresh fetches a whole page and
     replaces #cart's innerHTML; several files call it on a single cart change
     and the swaps stacked, each throwing away the paint before it. This wraps a
     plain theme function — unlike the fetch wrapper that broke the cart, there
     is no native binding involved. */
  function coalesce(){
    var fn = window.pgDrawerRefresh;
    if (typeof fn !== 'function' || fn.pgCoalesced) return;
    var inflight = null, queued = false;
    function run(){
      inflight = Promise.resolve(fn()).then(function(){
        inflight = null;
        if (queued){ queued = false; return run(); }
      }, function(){ inflight = null; });
      return inflight;
    }
    var w = function(){
      if (inflight){ queued = true; return inflight; }
      return run();
    };
    w.pgCoalesced = 1;
    window.pgDrawerRefresh = w;
  }

  function sync(){
    if (busy) return;
    var now = Date.now();
    if (now - lastRun < 1500) return;                   /* never hammer the cart */
    lastRun = now; busy = true;

    fetch('/cart.js', {headers: {'Accept': 'application/json'}})
      .then(function(r){ return r.json(); })
      .then(function(c){
        var consoles = 0, gift = null;
        (c.items || []).forEach(function(it){
          if (it.handle === CONSOLE) consoles += it.quantity;
          /* only the line THIS adds carries the property: a case the shopper
             paid for is never counted here and never touched */
          if (it.handle === CASE_HANDLE && it.properties && it.properties._free_gift && !gift) gift = it;
        });

        if (consoles > 0 && !gift){
          if (added) return;                        /* already tried once this page */
          added = true;
          return post('/cart/add.js', {items: [{id: GIFT_VARIANT, quantity: 1, properties: {_free_gift: 'yes'}}]})
            .then(function(r){ if (r && r.ok) refresh(); });
        }
        /* the corrections below never refresh: the drawer repaints itself, and
           a refresh here is what turns a correction into a visible churn */
        if (consoles > 0 && gift && gift.quantity > 1){
          return post('/cart/change.js', {id: gift.key, quantity: 1});
        }
        if (consoles === 0 && gift){
          return post('/cart/change.js', {id: gift.key, quantity: 0});
        }
      })
      .catch(function(){})
      .then(function(){ busy = false; });
  }

  function later(){ setTimeout(sync, 900); }

  /* the FREE GIFT pill: clear ftFix's inline measurement */
  function pill(){
    document.querySelectorAll('.pg-free-tag').forEach(function(el){
      if (el.style.textIndent) el.style.removeProperty('text-indent');
      if (el.style.width) el.style.removeProperty('width');
    });
  }

  function boot(){
    coalesce();
    pill();
    sync();

    /* anything that can change the cart, without patching anything global */
    document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
      var t = e.target;
      if (!t || !t.closest) return;
      if (t.closest('.pgx-atc, .pg-r36-atc, .pg-tt-atc, .pg-tadd, .pg-case-add2, .pgx-case-add, #cart .l4ca a.remove, #cart .input-amount, .pg-qbtn')) later();
    }, true);

    var c = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (c && window.MutationObserver){
      var q = false;
      new MutationObserver(function(){
        if (q) return;
        q = true;
        setTimeout(function(){ q = false; coalesce(); pill(); sync(); }, 400);
      }).observe(c, {childList: true, subtree: true});
    }
    [800, 2500, 6000].forEach(function(t){ setTimeout(function(){ coalesce(); pill(); sync(); }, t); });
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot); else boot();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Gift Fix", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG Gift Fix"}]}
{% endschema %}
